# React — Testing

Stack: **Vitest** + **React Testing Library** for units and integration, **Playwright** for E2E.

## The principle

> Test what the user does, not how the component does it.

Query by role, label, and visible text. `getByRole('button', { name: /save/i })` survives a
refactor; `container.querySelector('.btn-primary')` does not, and it never proved the button was
reachable in the first place.

## Priority of queries

1. `getByRole` — matches how assistive tech sees the app
2. `getByLabelText` — form fields
3. `getByPlaceholderText`, `getByText`
4. `getByTestId` — **last resort**, and it needs a reason

## Structure

```tsx
it('shows an error when the email is already taken', async () => {
  // arrange
  server.use(emailTakenHandler);
  render(<SignUpForm />);

  // act
  await user.type(screen.getByLabelText(/email/i), 'taken@example.com');
  await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /sign up/i }));

  // assert
  expect(await screen.findByText(/already registered/i)).toBeVisible();
});
```

- Test names say the behavior, not the function: *"shows an error when the email is already taken."*
- One behavior per test. A test that needs "and" in its name is two tests.
- `userEvent`, not `fireEvent` — it goes through the real event sequence.
- `findBy*` for anything async. Never `waitFor` wrapped around a bare `getBy*`.

## What to test

**Do:** user-visible behavior, conditional rendering, error and empty states, form validation,
accessibility of interactive elements, and every bug you fix (write the failing test first).

**Don't:** implementation details, internal state, third-party library internals, or a snapshot of
a whole page — a large snapshot fails on every change and gets approved without being read.

## Mocking

- Mock at the **network** boundary (MSW), not the module boundary. Mocking your own modules tests
  the mock.
- No mock in an E2E test. If it needs a mock, it is an integration test.
- Every mock is reset between tests. A leaking mock produces a passing suite that proves nothing.
